---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About FCMOBILETOOLS"
  description="About FCMOBILETOOLS, an independent FC Mobile fan resource built by TanzimFC for tools, game information, guides, reviews and community resources."
>
  <article class="wrap legal-page about-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / FCMOBILETOOLS</p>
    <h1>About FCMOBILETOOLS</h1>
    <p class="legal-lead">Last updated: October 9, 2026</p>

    <section class="about-intro">
      <h2>A fan project built around useful information.</h2>
      <p>
        FCMOBILETOOLS is an independent FC Mobile website created and maintained under the
        TanzimFC project. It brings together practical tools, live game resources, calculators,
        guides, reviews, event coverage, redeem-code information and other
        reference material for people who play FC Mobile.
      </p>
      <p>
        The idea behind the site is straightforward: instead of making players search across
        different pages for small pieces of information, keep useful resources in one place and
        make them easier to understand and use.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Why FCMOBILETOOLS exists</h2>
      <p>
        FC Mobile changes frequently. New events, player releases, rewards, ratings, redeem codes,
        seasons and gameplay-related information can make older guides difficult to rely on.
        FCMOBILETOOLS exists to provide a dedicated place for practical resources that can be
        updated as the game develops.
      </p>
      <p>
        The focus is not only on publishing news. The site is designed around things a player can
        actually use, whether that means checking an event, comparing information, planning a
        squad, calculating resources, reading a guide or checking whether a
        code is still worth trying.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. What you can find here</h2>
      <p>
        FCMOBILETOOLS covers several parts of the FC Mobile experience. The exact features and
        available pages can change over time, but the site is built around a few consistent areas:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Tools and calculators:</strong> utilities for team building, training, rank-ups, planning and other in-game decisions.</li>
        <li><strong>Live resources:</strong> events, redeem codes, season information and other time-sensitive game references.</li>
        <li><strong>Articles:</strong> updates, guides, reviews, analysis and longer-form FC Mobile coverage.</li>
        <li><strong>Community and account features:</strong> optional profiles, quests, XP and Tokens, surveys, achievements, leaderboards and other member progress tools.</li>
        <li><strong>Live community features:</strong> captain-tracker voting and published tournament brackets, fixtures and results where available.</li>
        <li><strong>Community resources:</strong> creator-focused content and selected community information that can help players discover useful work.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Tools are built for practical use</h2>
      <p>
        A calculator is most useful when it answers a real question quickly. FCMOBILETOOLS
        therefore treats tools as products in their own right rather than as decorative extras.
        Inputs should be understandable, results should be readable, and the interface should
        work across desktop and mobile screens.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tool results are based on the data, rules and assumptions implemented by each feature.
        They are intended to help with planning and reference, not to represent an official EA
        account calculation or guarantee a particular in-game outcome.
      </p>
    </section>


    <section>
      <h2>4. Live events and changing information</h2>
      <p>
        Event pages and other live resources are designed around information that can change
        quickly. Dates, rewards, requirements, availability, redeem codes and related details may
        change after a game update or an official announcement.
      </p>
      <p>
        For that reason, a page being published on FCMOBILETOOLS does not mean every detail will
        remain current forever. We aim to update useful resources as information changes and to
        make outdated information easier to identify and correct.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. How we approach articles and updates</h2>
      <p>
        FCMOBILETOOLS publishes several kinds of editorial content, including news-style updates,
        guides, reviews and analysis. These formats are different from one another and should be
        read with their context in mind.
      </p>
      <p>
        Official announcements are treated differently from community reports, leaks and
        interpretation. A community report can be useful without being a confirmed EA statement,
        and an analytical article can discuss possibilities without turning them into established
        facts. The site aims to preserve those distinctions rather than blur them together.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Sources and verification</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on the subject, information may come from official EA or FC Mobile material,
        public game information, community reporting, creator information, public reference
        resources and other sources relevant to the topic.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sources are not automatically equal in certainty. When a distinction matters, the site
        aims to identify what is confirmed, what is reported by the community, and what is analysis
        or interpretation. Readers should use official EA channels for information where an
        authoritative source is specifically required.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Reviews and community votes are separate</h2>
      <p>
        FCMOBILETOOLS may publish player reviews and other editorial assessments to help readers
        understand how a card or player can perform within the context of FC Mobile.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reviews are editorial resources, not official EA ratings and not a substitute for a
        player's own preferences, team setup or play style. Separate community tracker votes may
        show users' picks, but they do not determine an editorial review's conclusion.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. The project and its creator</h2>
      <p>
        FCMOBILETOOLS is built and maintained under the TanzimFC project. TanzimFC is responsible
        for the site's direction, tools, editorial work and ongoing development.
      </p>
      <p>
        The project may also include contributions from other creators or community members.
        Contributor participation can vary over time, and publication does not mean that every
        contributor represents TanzimFC or speaks for the site on every subject.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/creator/">Learn more about the creator and contributor programme ↗</a></p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Independent from EA SPORTS FC Mobile</h2>
      <p>
        FCMOBILETOOLS is an independent fan-made website. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
        sponsored by, or officially connected to Electronic Arts, EA SPORTS or FC Mobile.
      </p>
      <p>
        EA SPORTS, Electronic Arts, FC Mobile, player names, logos, game assets, trademarks and
        other third-party material remain the property of their respective owners. Their presence
        on this website does not mean that FCMOBILETOOLS owns those rights or that a third party
        officially supports the project.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Original site work and third-party material</h2>
      <p>
        FCMOBILETOOLS includes original code, interface work, editorial writing, tool logic and
        other material created for the project, alongside third-party or game-related material
        that may be referenced or displayed for fan and informational purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Third-party rights remain with their respective owners. For more detail about rights,
        attribution, creator submissions and copyright concerns, see the site's
        <a href="/legal/copyright">Copyright &amp; Intellectual Property</a> page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>11. Accuracy, corrections and updates</h2>
      <p>
        We try to keep useful pages accurate, but FC Mobile is a changing game and errors can
        happen. A player value can change, a redeem code can expire, an event can move, a link can
        break, or a source can later prove to have been incomplete.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you notice something that should be corrected, please send the page or feature name,
        the relevant URL, a short explanation and supporting information when available. Useful
        corrections help improve the resource for everyone.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/legal/contact">Send a correction or contact FCMOBILETOOLS ↗</a></p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>12. What FCMOBILETOOLS does not claim</h2>
      <p>
        The site does not claim to be an official EA support channel, an official game database,
        an official source for every piece of FC Mobile information, or a guarantee that a
        calculator result, player recommendation, community vote, tournament result or event
        detail will produce a particular outcome in the game. Site XP and Tokens are not official
        FC Mobile currency or in-game rewards.
      </p>
      <p>
        For account recovery, bans, purchases, refunds, payment problems and other account or
        service matters, use the appropriate official EA support resources.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>13. Built for the FC Mobile community</h2>
      <p>
        At its core, FCMOBILETOOLS is a resource project. The goal is to reduce friction for
        players by turning scattered information and repetitive calculations into pages and tools
        that are easier to use.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site will continue to evolve as FC Mobile evolves. New tools, articles and community-focused features can be added when they provide
        a useful reason to exist.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-links">
      <h2>Explore FCMOBILETOOLS</h2>
      <div class="legal-links">
        <a href="/team-ovr/">Team OVR</a>
        <a href="/football-centre/">Football Centre</a>
        <a href="/events/">Events</a>
        <a href="/blog/">Articles &amp; Guides</a>
        <a href="/legal/contact">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-disclaimer">
      <h2>A note on the site's legal pages</h2>
      <p>
        This About page explains what FCMOBILETOOLS is and how the project is organized. It does
        not replace the site's <a href="/legal/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>,
        <a href="/legal/terms-of-use">Terms of Use</a>,
        <a href="/legal/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>,
        <a href="/legal/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>, or
        <a href="/legal/copyright">Copyright &amp; Intellectual Property</a> pages.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.about-page ul{margin:14px 0 0 20px;padding:0;color:#aab6c4;font-size:14px;line-height:1.85}
.about-page li{padding-left:5px;margin-bottom:8px}
.about-page li strong{color:#dce7ef}
.about-intro{
  margin:0 0 8px;
  padding:22px 24px;
  border:1px solid #294454;
  border-radius:16px;
  background:linear-gradient(145deg,#0d1b24,#081118);
}
.about-intro h2{font-size:23px!important;margin-bottom:12px!important}
.about-intro p{font-size:14px!important}
.about-page section p+p{margin-top:12px}
.about-page section>p:last-child a,
.about-page section a{font-weight:600}
.about-links .legal-links{margin-top:4px}
.about-disclaimer{margin-top:8px}
.about-disclaimer p{font-size:13px}
@media(max-width:560px){
  .about-intro{padding:19px}
  .about-page ul{margin-left:17px;font-size:13.5px}
}
</style>
